    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This is the Electronic Supplement of the data used to produce the results of the paper by Ceferino et al. (2018). The paper evaluates the earthquake casualties resulting from an earthquake of magnitude 8.8 occurring in the Coast of Lima, in Peru. The Electronic Supplement contains the information on the Earthquake Event, the Building Structural Typology, and the Building Occupancy Dynamics as vector and raster files. The Electronic Supplement also provides the building typology list, the building typology map to HAZUS, and the relative gross area per building typology in Excel files.\r\n\r\nReference:\r\nCeferino, L., Kiremidjian, A. & Deierlein, G. (2018). Regional Multi-severity Casualty Estimation Due to Building Damage Following a Mw 8.8 Earthquake Scenario in Lima, Peru. Earthquake Spectra.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Ceferino, L., Kiremidjian, A., and Deierlein, G. (2018) Data on building exposure and vulnerability in a 1 km x 1km grid for Lima, Peru, for earthquake casualty evaluation. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/dn034gd9112",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
